  "steps": [
   {
    "id": 1021153,
    "guid": "069A81C9FB5D4E259F4D30BA04E53356",
    "previous_id": null,
    "previous_guid": null,
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Sample collection:\n\u2022Collect saliva in a disposable pipet by haveing the subject placing the squeezed pipet into subject&#39;s mouth and releasing pressure on the bulb, with patient directing the pipet to the pooled saliva in the mouth.This will collect  1 mL  to  2.5 \u00b5L  of sample.\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019438,
    "number": "1",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021154,
    "guid": "DECE288C52784F43A10AC824C4C999AB",
    "previous_id": 1021153,
    "previous_guid": "069A81C9FB5D4E259F4D30BA04E53356",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Sample processing:\n\u2022~ 1.5 \u00b5L  of this sample is moved from the pipet into a 1.5 ml centrifuge tube. \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019442,
    "number": "2",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021155,
    "guid": "D8047A02B71E47EABB8C9BDB261CA8E9",
    "previous_id": 1021154,
    "previous_guid": "DECE288C52784F43A10AC824C4C999AB",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\u2022 200 \u00b5L  of this sample is moved to a clean and empty 1.5ml centrifuge tube and mixed with  800 \u00b5L  of RO water.\n\ngreatly reduced viscosity,   the amount of sample may be reduced if the saliva is highly viscous.\n \n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019443,
    "number": "3",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021156,
    "guid": "B2F1FC54AC2A4FA28E8A5818F1829074",
    "previous_id": 1021155,
    "previous_guid": "D8047A02B71E47EABB8C9BDB261CA8E9",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\u2022Sample is then agitated for  00:00:05  to  00:00:15  to mix.   \n\neven mix, \n \n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019446,
    "number": "4",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021157,
    "guid": "014B65344E434A9293443D5CE2BE0366",
    "previous_id": 1021156,
    "previous_guid": "B2F1FC54AC2A4FA28E8A5818F1829074",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\u2022Sample is then placed into a 3 ml disposable syringe with a o.45um MCE filter attached and the sample is then filtered into a new 1.5 centrifuge tube. \n\nThis removes the possible mouth contaminates that can potentially clog the instrument capillary.\n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019447,
    "number": "5",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021158,
    "guid": "421B6C4102E844B5BE4FB7CBC637316B",
    "previous_id": 1021157,
    "previous_guid": "014B65344E434A9293443D5CE2BE0366",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\u2022This filtered sample is then placed into the IVDS sample holder.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019448,
    "number": "6",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021159,
    "guid": "72D3305D04314D139352B2A24BCEC8B5",
    "previous_id": 1021158,
    "previous_guid": "421B6C4102E844B5BE4FB7CBC637316B",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\u2022Instrument saturates for  00:00:30   to   00:01:00  and then initiated for instrument scan (testing).Test is 1 scan of 1.5 minutes and sample is processed at 40nl per minute. Test results are a real time read out from IVDS.Data is stored automatically.Sample is assigned a number for processing, this thesampleidwhichwillmatchsourceid.\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019452,
    "number": "7",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021160,
    "guid": "D9653F4E16F94ED9BD8B562DCE6E476B",
    "previous_id": 1021159,
    "previous_guid": "72D3305D04314D139352B2A24BCEC8B5",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "If the sample does not have enough ionization salt naturally from the saliva, then adding ammonium acetate  ( 50 \u00b5L  @  20 millimolar (mM) ) is placed in the sample and vortexed for  00:00:05  to 00:00:15  and rerun.  (Determined by the voltage and Taylor cone shape.)\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019449,
    "number": "8",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021161,
    "guid": "D4AE23CD1B424229A7CB3A6A440B37ED",
    "previous_id": 1021160,
    "previous_guid": "D9653F4E16F94ED9BD8B562DCE6E476B",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Instrument setup:\n\u2022Air is set to 4psi\n\u2022CO2and Air flow are set to 2.5 and 1.5 lpm respectively.\n\u2022nA is typically set to -300nA and the kV is typically set to 2.05 . These are set to balance the Taylor cone on the ESI.\n\u2022Scan is set to  00:01:30  and set for 1 to 2 scans as needed.  (View Results)\n\u2022Other instrument settings are per standard setting in the operators guide.\n\u2022These settings do not change for the days run, regardless of the number of samples run.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019454,
    "number": "9",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021162,
    "guid": "F1B27445E5F6454BAE19BE846299DA04",
    "previous_id": 1021161,
    "previous_guid": "D4AE23CD1B424229A7CB3A6A440B37ED",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "After each sample processing:\n\u2022After a positive test a  1.5 \u00b5L  of blank buffer is placed into the instrument tube holder and is run as a blank test with the same settings as a sample.This will flush the instrument and the readout will have a zero reading.If not then repeat.\n\u2022A sample that has a negative result, proceed to the next sample, a flush is not necessary.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019456,
    "number": "10",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021163,
    "guid": "6EA9254A49C043979EC889DB78BA993D",
    "previous_id": 1021162,
    "previous_guid": "F1B27445E5F6454BAE19BE846299DA04",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "At the end of the day run:\nClean the instrument with Potassium Hydroxide  20 millimolar (mM)  solution in a 1.5 ml centrifuge tube flowing into the instrument for  00:02:00  .\nRemove clean vial and Reverse air flow for  00:02:00  and then return to normal.\nRun a buffer sample for  00:01:00  to verify instrument has no counts or is clean.\nRemove buffer and reverse air flow for  00:02:00 , return to normal air flow for  00:10:00 .Shut off instrument, air supply, CO2, and electrical.\n\n\n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019457,
    "number": "11",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1021164,
    "guid": "CBBE6D971E864AC0B1A6B7150FF4ADBB",
    "previous_id": 1021163,
    "previous_guid": "6EA9254A49C043979EC889DB78BA993D",
    "section": "<p>Collection</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "\n Integrated Virus Detection System (Non Specific Virus Detector, TSI, Inc, 3081, 3480, 3080, 3772, 3032, components;  3081 - DMA, 3480 - Electrospray Generator,  3080 - Electrostatic Classifier, 3772 - Condensation Particle Counter, 3032 - vacuum pump.) \n\n\na negative result will display as no counts by the cpc for the determined &#34;size&#34; or m/z ratio.   A positive result is a cpc count at the determined &#34;size&#34; or m/z ratio.  It is unknown to determine if there is an active infection since it is unknown what the minimum number of virions are needed to start an infection, so we simply detect them and count the virus particles and not the copies of gentic material that are a secondary detection if at all. \n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41548,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 1019567,
    "number": "12",
    "cases": [],
